1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Hello, I am Zhanzhol.
We are group SE-2623.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Campus Lost and Found helps students
search for missing items

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,000
and share found objects.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,000
This is our running local prototype.

5
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:20,000
I search for a notebook,
open a matching notice,

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,000
and check its location and status.
These are fictional classroom accounts.

7
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:30,000
An astanait.edu.kz address in this demo
does not prove university identity,

8
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,000
and real university sign-in
is not connected.

9
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:40,000
For my formats section, I compare the same
project image as PNG, JPEG and WebP.

10
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:43,000
PNG preserves every pixel.

11
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:47,000
Lossy compression trades some detail
for smaller files.

12
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:50,000
SVG keeps the logo sharp.

13
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:54,000
I am Daniil. My part integrates the media
and measures their cost.

14
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:59,000
The page uses local WebP images
and an SVG logo.

15
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:05,000
At a narrow screen width,
images fit the layout.

16
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:09,000
Now I post a found bottle.
I choose its category

17
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:13,000
and add a title, description,
location and date.

18
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:17,000
I press Publish notice.
The success message confirms the change.

19
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Refreshing the page shows
that the notice remains saved.

20
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:30,000
We compare the same page before and after
optimisation with cache disabled

21
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,000
and Fast 4G throttling.

22
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:36,000
Our evidence records transferred bytes,
request count and loading time.

23
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Page loading is different
from the search performance requirement.

24
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:44,000
I am Daulet. My part covers
accessibility and the video.

25
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:49,000
I mark this notice as returned.
The result appears as text,

26
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:53,000
so sound is unnecessary.
The success animation respects reduced motion.

27
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:59,000
Meaningful images have alternative text,

28
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:05,000
while decorative images
have empty alternative text.

29
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:11,000
This diagram shows the browser, the Flask
application running with Waitress,

30
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:16,000
and the SQLite database on one computer.
Images are local files.

31
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:21,000
Our video includes each member's
own voice and English subtitles.

32
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:26,000
This remains a local demo
with test accounts,

33
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:30,000
without real university sign-in
or outgoing email.
